codex
Implemented the Windows Credential Manager backend and storage facade in [windows_store.rs](/home/abdel/Documents/Coding/binus-cli/spikes/001-auth/src/windows_store.rs). It uses fixed primary and candidate targets, bounded JSON blobs, sanitized native errors, and the reviewed SID-scoped lock for complete storage operations. Shared record types remain publicly re-exported, and `Debug` redacts account, token, and role values. Linux storage stays on its existing Unix path.

**Checks:** the full Linux test suite, formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, and Linux release build passed. The isolated store and lock sources passed Windows target checks with warnings denied. The main crate’s Windows check still fails on Unix filesystem, process, signal, and permission-test code; that output is recorded in [the evidence file](/home/abdel/Documents/Coding/binus-cli/.agent/windows-store-impl-evidence.md). This does not establish full Windows CLI support.

Native Windows execution remains pending. I did not access real credentials or run login, browser, or API operations. Relevant files were already modified in the shared worktree at the start, so exact pre-task working-tree hashes were unavailable; the evidence records that limitation and the available Git baseline. No commit or publication was made.
